From: rnsbox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] licheervnano-arm64: reclock the uarts — exact 2 Mbaud SLIP

The arm64 LicheeRV Nano board (added by 0019) inherited soph_base_arm's
uarts verbatim: 8250 with a hardcoded clock-frequency of 25 MHz, so the
SLIP link to the HaLow modem was limited to 1,562,500 baud.

Reclock the SoC in of_clk_init, before any driver probes: disppll
1188 -> 768 MHz (the LUT row now comes from the shared licheerv-nano
0045), clk_cam0_200 -> disppll/8 = 96 MHz. Every dw-uart is a gate-only
child of clk_cam0_200, so the 8250 input becomes 96 MHz and the modem's
factory 2 Mbaud is exact (96M/16/3). Both uart0 (console) and uart1
(SLIP) must take their rate from the CCF, so delete the stale 25 MHz
clock-frequency; without that the console dies 3.84x at the first
reclock. The XGPIOA[28]/[29] pinmux for UART1 is already in the board's
u-boot cvi_board_init.c (0019).

The 2 Mbaud slip.conf/S31slip default is carried by the shared
licheerv-nano 0047; the arm series' redundant 0007 (LUT) and 0010
(default flip) are dropped in the same commit.
diff --git a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_licheervnano_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2002_licheervnano_arm64_sd.dts b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_licheervnano_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2002_licheervnano_arm64_sd.dts
index b6b78e1..a3c8577 100644
--- a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_licheervnano_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2002_licheervnano_arm64_sd.dts
+++ b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_licheervnano_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2002_licheervnano_arm64_sd.dts
@@ -57,8 +57,29 @@
         status = "okay";
 };
 
+// RNSBox: reclock disppll 1188 -> 768 MHz and clk_cam0_200 osc/1 ->
+// disppll/8 = 96 MHz (of_clk_init, before any driver probes). Every
+// dw-uart is a gate-only child of clk_cam0_200, so the 8250 input
+// becomes 96 MHz: 2 Mbaud is exact (96M/16/3), 1 Mbaud too (quot 6).
+// The 8250 must take the rate from the CCF; the stale 25 MHz
+// clock-frequency is deleted below or the console dies 3.84x.
+&clk {
+	assigned-clocks = <&clk CV181X_CLK_DISPPLL>, <&clk CV181X_CLK_CAM0_200>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <0>, <&clk CV181X_CLK_DISPPLL>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <768000000>, <96000000>;
+};
+
+&uart0 {
+	clocks = <&clk CV181X_CLK_UART0>;
+	/delete-property/ clock-frequency;
+};
+
+// SLIP to the HaLow modem (S31slip, /dev/ttyS1); the pads are muxed to
+// UART1 TX/RX by u-boot (cvi_board_init.c, GPIOA 28/29).
 &uart1 {
         status = "okay";
+        clocks = <&clk CV181X_CLK_UART1>;
+        /delete-property/ clock-frequency;
 };
 
 &pwm0 {
